    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d1385">

                <pb facs="0920" n="804" xml:id="pg804"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">File No. 312.52/227.</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">Special Agent Carothers
                        to the Secretary of State.</hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#center">[Telegrams.]</seg>
                </opener>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">El Paso</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1914-04-11T19:00:00-07:00">
                            <hi rendition="#italic">April 11, 1914, 7 p.m.</hi>
                        </date>
                    </dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>Fearing that Carranza would depart without arriving at a definite understanding
                    regarding representations made through Department of State in interest of
                    foreigners not Americans, I last night delivered him in writing a request that
                    he reply to the several representations I have made, and that he make a definite
                    statement as to his intentions in future on similar representations. This
                    afternoon I held conference with Pesqueira at his request. He informed me he and
                    Carranza had discussed matter of my request, and that I may assure you that
                    Carranza has agreed to accept them upon your statement that representations are
                    made at request of foreign government. This will clear up situation, and I hope
                    for telegraphic reply to my several communications. With few exceptions,
                    Carranza officials and all of Villa’s men do not agree with Carranza on his
                    attitude in opposing the mediation of United States regarding foreigners, and
                    many have openly expressed their discontent. I hope for complete understanding
                    between Carranza and Villa in Chihuahua next week.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">G. C. Carothers</hi></signed>.</closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
